# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored — never commit
# credentials.
#
# Authentication is handled by the commercetools CLI, NOT by this file. Run
# `commercetools auth login` once (see the README) — the integration-layer commands
# (`validate` / `push` / `status` / `delete`, `schema *`, `config *`) reuse that
# login token (a `manage_project` principal) and read the target project key from the
# login context. There are no client credentials here anymore.

# OPTIONAL. Override the integration layer edge base URL. Normally you don't set this;
# leave it unset to use the deployed instance, or point it at a local/staging edge
# (e.g. http://localhost:8080) for development.
# INTEGRATION_LAYER_URL=https://integration-layer.stage.europe-west1.gcp.commercetools.com

# OPTIONAL. Local-only config for `commercetools integration-layer extension serve` /
# `... invoke`: there is no integration layer to read `ctx.config` from locally, so
# each `EXTENSION_CONFIG_<KEY>` var is exposed to your handlers/resolvers as
# `ctx.config.<KEY>`. Example:
# EXTENSION_CONFIG_BLOCKED_SKU=BLOCKED-SKU
